Subject: [PATCH] encode: keep two pictures in flight and add vaSyncBuffer

EndPicture queued the input, waited for the coded picture and for the input
to come back, so the encoder sat idle from the end of one picture until the
client had read it, uploaded the next input and called EndPicture again.
Queue the picture and return instead; collect it when the client syncs the
coded buffer (new vaSyncBuffer, vaMapBuffer), syncs or reads the input
surface, or when a later EndPicture needs its CAPTURE buffer (two in
flight, one per CAPTURE buffer). FFmpeg switches to its async path (default
async_depth 2) only when vaSyncBuffer is implemented.
Rate control, forced key frames and a new geometry first collect what is
queued. Contexts beyond the first 8 encoders keep one picture at a time.
